<title>VENEZUELA: Amoco joins Sivensa in Venezuelan oil bidding.</title>
<headline>Amoco joins Sivensa in Venezuelan oil bidding.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amoco and Venezuela's steel company Sivensa have signed a letter of intent to form a consortium to participate in Venezuela's third round of oil operating licences to be awarded in June, a Sivensa spokesman said Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We signed the letter about a month ago. We will be the only two companies in the consortium,&quot; Sivensa director Neil Malloy told Reuters.</p>
<p>The licenses to operate oilfields as contractor for state- owned Petroleos de Venezuela are open to competitive bidding and the winners are expected to be announced in the first week of June.</p>
<p>((--Ana Isabel Martinez, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2611))</p>
